0,Music of Mali - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Mali,"April 20, 2026 - The ethnomusicologist Ryan Skinner ... of music and politics in contemporary Mali. The Malinké, Soninke - Sarakole, Dyula and Bambara peoples form the core of Malian culture, but the region of the Mali Empire has been extended far to the north in present-day Mali, where Tuareg and Maure peoples continue a largely nomadic desert culture. In the east Songhay, Bozo ...",Mali,East New Britain
1,Mali Music (singer) - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mali_Music_(singer),"February 8, 2026 - Kortney Jamaal Pollard (born January 12, 1988), known professionally as Mali Music, is an American singer-songwriter and record producer from Savannah, Georgia. His first two studio albums, The Coming (2008) and The 2econd Coming (2009) were released independently through ByStorm Records and ...",Mali,East New Britain
2,MUSIC; Unexpected Pairings Via Britain and Mali - The New York Times,https://www.nytimes.com/2002/08/04/arts/music-unexpected-pairings-via-britain-and-mali.html,"August 4, 2002 - The release of ''Mali Music'' in Britain, in the spring, inspired yet another round of abuse from Mr. Albarn's old foes (and rivals) in Oasis, the British rock group that wears its traditionalism with pride. In one interview, the group's guitarist Noel Gallagher seemed to purposely misstate the country that Mr.",Mali,East New Britain
